<!--
  5-axis dental mill (900d) - simple box model for test-only visualization.
  Spindle side: base -> column -> X (left/right) -> Z (up/down)
  Table side  : base -> Y (front/back) -> B (tilt about the left/right axis) -> C (platter rotation)
  Frames: x = viewer's right, y = away from the viewer (toward the column), z = up, so the ROS axes match the
  machine axis names. Part sizes are rough guesses from a photo.

  Joint values are machine units (m, rad) with home (the home switch) = 0. Motor revs -> joint value uses the
  placeholders below; lead and gear ratio are NOT known yet, and of the motor directions only Y is known
  (docs/hardware/축 정리.md).

  The layout follows the limits (2026-10-21), so it stays consistent when the lead changes:
    - at mid-travel of X and of Y the tool is above the C axis
    - at the Z - limit (lowest) the tool tip is tool_clear above the workpiece top (B = 0)
    - the X beam covers the carriage over the whole X travel, the base covers the table over the whole Y travel,
      and the column stays behind the table at the motor + end of Y (DI16, Y - limit)
  Check with ros2_sim/verify_limits.sh. Visual names are used by scripts/verify_limits.py.
-->
<robot name="teeth_mill">
  <!-- tool tip above the workpiece at the Z - limit -->
  <!-- ===== colors ===== -->
  <material name="frame">
    <color rgba="0.15 0.15 0.17 1"/>
  </material>
  <material name="alu">
    <color rgba="0.78 0.79 0.80 1"/>
  </material>
  <material name="cast">
    <color rgba="0.33 0.35 0.38 1"/>
  </material>
